Subject: rules_search ranks rare terms and terms close together first

Found in the assistant tool review of the live gateway (2026-10-28):
"commander damage" did not have 903.10a (21 combat damage from one commander)
in the top 5: "damage" is in hundreds of rules and counted as much as
"commander". The score now weighs each term by how rare it is in the rules,
counts at most 3 uses of a term, doubles it when every term stands within a
few words of the others, and adds a quarter when a term names the rule's
section (903 Commander). The phrase bonus and the all-terms bonus stay, as
does the total (entries with any one of the terms). The documents' tokens
and term counts are worked out once per index.

On the vendored Comprehensive Rules, "commander damage" now has 704.6c and
903.10a in its top 5 and "commander tax" leads with 903.8 and the glossary's
Commander Tax; the upstream ranking tests still pass.

tests/test_rules_search_ranking.py.

Upstream: Kautiontape/mystic-forge at dd82cd1 has none of these. Needs
patches 0001-0016 applied first.
